{
  "description": "Evidence-bound criteria for the harness scorecard (A1 to A17). Read by tooling/scorecard.js. Fixture criteria carry weight 8 per aspect and the operational criterion weight 2, so an aspect proven only by fixtures scores at most 8, and 9 or 10 need operational evidence. A criterion whose suite does not exist yet stays UNKNOWN until its package lands. Policy frozen 2026-10-14, before evaluation. Amended 2026-10-14 after the overnight Brain stall: A9 adds mission-stall and splits its fixture weight 3, 3 and 2. An amendment may add evidence, never remove it. Amended 2026-10-16: credential-boundary is owner-held, because its package N5 narrows the deploy credential the owner chose to keep on 2026-09-23. It keeps its weight 2 and counts zero, so no score rises and A3 is capped at 8 while that decision stands. Amended 2026-10-19: every operational window criterion gains a probe, tooling/window-probe.js <id>, which grades the 14 complete UTC days before the run from records the harness writes, per tooling/window-specs.js. A day counts only from the day its writer first recorded that evidence completely, nothing is backfilled, and a need no writer records fails by name. The amendment adds evidence only: no need, weight or 14-day span is removed or shortened. gate-evidence also watches the real plugins/autodev-core/scripts/gate-records.js; the tooling/ path it named never existed, so the writer could change unseen. Amended 2026-10-29: instruction-window lets a config profile be retired. A profile directory whose logs/instruction-envelope.retired.json names a retiredAt day and a reason stops being required from that day on, and every earlier day still needs its records. A marker the profile outlives, with any record on or after retiredAt, is ignored. This removes no evidence a running profile can write: a login nobody uses loads no instructions, so requiring its records made the criterion unreachable rather than stricter.",
